WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.412
The analytical reasoning in this module transfers
well across database systems but

00:00:04.438 --> 00:00:10.150
the exact syntax may change For example PostgreSQL
can subtract timestamps

00:00:10.175 --> 00:00:14.650
directly to create an interval Some other systems
use functions such as

00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:21.062
DATEDIFF instead PostgreSQL supports FILTER for
conditional aggregates Other

00:00:21.088 --> 00:00:24.362
systems may not so SUM with CASE is often a more
portable

00:00:24.375 --> 00:00:29.862
replacement Support for ROLLUP CUBE GROUPING SETS
and even some window syntax

00:00:29.875 --> 00:00:33.812
can also vary by product and version The important
lesson is to

00:00:33.838 --> 00:00:38.738
transfer the reasoning before transferring the
syntax The reasoning is define the

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:43.675
source population filter rows choose the grain
calculate measures apply group thresholds

00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:48.150
and sort the report When you move from PostgreSQL to
another engine

00:00:48.362 --> 00:00:53.375
consult that engine's documentation for the exact
functions and syntax Do not

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:57.862
assume every database implements every feature in
the same way If you

00:00:57.875 --> 00:01:02.188
understand the analytical structure of the query
adapting the syntax is usually

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.838
much easier than trying to memorize separate
solutions for every platform
